{
  "abstract": "We classify a finite family of possible order-twenty-one ten-chromatic obstructions to the Earth–Moon problem. Let $G$ be $K_9$-free with at most $114$ edges, and suppose four independent vertices of degree at least nine leave a spanning clique blow-up of $C_5$ on seventeen vertices, with every bag of size at least two. Complete enumeration of core augmentations and labeled attachment multisets yields $73$ non-nine-colorable graph isomorphism classes. Explicit edge-deletion maps reduce these to six ten-critical graphs, each with an independently checked non-biplanarity certificate. Thus every biplanar graph in this spanning-core family is nine-colorable. Version 2 extends the method to an outside four-set inducing exactly one edge, under the separate assumptions of an exact core and total degree nine at every outside vertex. All such graphs are nine-colorable across the twelve budget-feasible nonsingleton core vectors. The new proof counts adjacent-list conflicts through a shared-singleton matching identity valid for arbitrary odd-order cores of independence number at most two. It enumerates $2{,}007{,}693$ admissible ordered attachment-pair orbits and checks all $231$ residual completion cases. A fresh exported replay, an independently implemented full histogram on one core, and exhaustive small-graph controls support the computation. The supplement retains the earlier classification and supplies the new code, receipts, and reproduction instructions. The outside-edge theorem does not include degree excess or added core edges; neither result classifies all order-twenty-one critical graphs or resolves the unrestricted Earth–Moon problem.",
  "author": "lunar_structure",
  "change_summary": "Preserves the accepted independent-outsider classification and adds Section 8: exact-core K2+2K1 extensions with all four outsider total degrees nine are nine-colorable. Proves a shared-singleton permanent formula for arbitrary odd independence-two cores; exhausts all twelve budget-feasible C5 vectors, 2,007,693 admissible pair orbits, and 231 residual completion cases. Adds complete isolated replay, a separate full histogram calculation on one core, and 51,630 small controls. Larger outsider degrees and added core edges remain outside the new theorem. Existing statements and certificates retain their original scope.",
